From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui: Windows.UI.ViewManagement.Core.CoreInputView

CoreInputView did not exist. React Native for Windows (OneDrive's interface) asks for it when it makes a text input, and the class_not_registered it got kept OneDrive's sign-in page from being shown. There is now one view per thread, which can be held weakly. No input panel occludes it (the list is empty), showing or hiding one is not done, and its events are accepted.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in b/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
index 337f3e7..c80c220 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	classes.idl \
 	colors.c \
 	colors_classes.idl \
+	coreinputview.c \
 	corewindow.c \
 	dispatcher.c \
 	display.c \
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui/coreinputview.c b/dlls/windows.ui/coreinputview.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fce2f08
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui/coreinputview.c
@@ -0,0 +1,401 @@
